Two bugs must be fixed in /gin/context.go. Do them one at a time and verify each.

BUG A (function `NegotiateFormat`, around line 1120): the matching loop is

			i := 0
			for ; i < len(accepted); i++ {
				if accepted[i] == '*' || offer[i] == '*' {
					return offer
				}
				if accepted[i] != offer[i] {
					break
				}
			}
			if i == len(accepted) {
				return offer
			}

When an offered format is a proper prefix of the accepted format (e.g. Accept: "text/html" and offered "text"), `offer[i]` is indexed past the end of `offer` and the library panics with "index out of range". Fix by bounding the loop: `for ; i < len(accepted) && i < len(offer); i++ {` — change nothing else in the function.

BUG B (function `FileAttachment`, around line 1039): the ASCII branch writes the filename into the Content-Disposition header unescaped:

		c.Writer.Header().Set("Content-Disposition", `attachment; filename="`+filename+`"`)

A filename containing a double quote or backslash produces a malformed header (header injection). Fix: escape it, i.e. use `escapeQuotes(filename)` in that branch, and add this helper to /gin/context.go (put it right above FileAttachment):

var quoteEscaper = strings.NewReplacer("\\", "\\\\", `"`, "\\\"`)

func escapeQuotes(s string) string {
	return quoteEscaper.Replace(s)
}

(that is: a package-level `var quoteEscaper = strings.NewReplacer("\\", "\\\\", "\"", "\\\"")` and `func escapeQuotes(s string) string { return quoteEscaper.Replace(s) }`). Make sure `strings` is already imported in context.go (it is). Do not change the non-ASCII branch.

VERIFICATION for both (run and report verbatim):
1. cd /gin && gofmt -l context.go (must print nothing)
2. cd /gin && go build ./... && go vet ./... 2>&1 | tail -20
3. cd /gin && go test -run 'TestContextNegotiation|TestContextRender' -v . 2>&1 | tail -40 (all must PASS)
4. Create a TEMPORARY test file /gin/zz_tmp_ctx_test.go in package gin:

package gin

import (
	"net/http"
	"net/http/httptest"
	"testing"

	"github.com/stretchr/testify/assert"
)

func TestTmpNegotiationFormatPrefix(t *testing.T) {
	c, _ := CreateTestContext(httptest.NewRecorder())
	c.Request, _ = http.NewRequest("POST", "", nil)
	c.Request.Header.Add("Accept", "text/html")
	assert.Empty(t, c.NegotiateFormat("text"))
	assert.Equal(t, MIMEHTML, c.NegotiateFormat(MIMEHTML))
}

func TestTmpEscapeAttachment(t *testing.T) {
	c, _ := CreateTestContext(httptest.NewRecorder())
	c.Request, _ = http.NewRequest("GET", "/", nil)
	c.FileAttachment("./testdata/hello.txt", `a"b.txt`)
	assert.Equal(t, `attachment; filename="a\"b.txt"`, c.Writer.Header().Get("Content-Disposition"))
}

